{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like","id":1295977,"title":"Your Favourite Convention Defects to the Traditions; What Does That Look Like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-11T16:47:09-07:00","id":1295977,"title":"Your Favourite Convention Defects to the Traditions; What Does That Look Like?","content":"We've seen two Conventions defect to the Traditions; why not another?<br /> <br /> To me, the two most viable candidates are the Void Engineers and the Syndicate. Both are relatively accepting of Reality Deviance as a fact of existence that needs to be worked with and around, not ignored or destroyed. The CEO who hires Ronin Garou to perform assaults on dangerous supernaturals, the Umbral Voyager who works alongside quirky &quot;aliens&quot;. Any Syndicate operatives who remained would be subsumed by the NWO, while Void Engineers who remained would likely fit best into Iteration X.<br /> <br /> UMBRAL ENGINEERS - attached to the Society of Ether<br /> <br /> Common Affinity Spheres: Dimensional Science<br /> <br /> Picture the VEs, but actually happy, and you have the Umbral Engineers. Freed to explore and work as they see fit, they make allies of various umbral travelers and are shown paths and ways that were hidden to them until now. Furthermore, they begin to learn some animistic reverence... although they wouldn't call it that! They begin to see that Dimensional Anomalies and Aliens are very fond of gifts, and that working with that is simply part of the scientific method. After all, there's nothing unscientific about the idea that people like gifts and that they're more likely to work with you if you provide them; why should it be any different with the Umbrae?<br /> <br /> SYNDICATE 2.0 - attached to the Virtual Adepts<br /> <br /> Common Affinity Spheres: Primal Utility, Mind, Data<br /> <br /> The Syndicate remains as it ever was... superficially they've rebranded, and they are a &quot;conscientious and caring financial institution&quot;. Much more emphasis on charity, equality in economic growth and fiscal fairness. In truth the Syndicate is as it ever was, and in many ways that is a good thing for the Traditions. This betrayal of the Technocracy likely has nothing to do with joining the Traditions, and everything to do with leaving the Technocracy... it's all about a civil war with the New World Order. The Syndicate didn't want a full-scale bloodbath, so they simply picked up their ball and went home. This way they can wage war by proxy, funding the highly motivated Traditions to take down their enemies.<br /> <br /> This new Syndicate is more open to mystical practices which work well with the &quot;modern mysticism&quot; they had managed to pass as Mutual Science within the Union. The corporate world is full of strange superstitions, and free from the stifling orthodoxy of the Technocracy the Syndicate can explore these 21st Century Rituals in peace. Their newfound link with the VAs means new ventures in Cryptocurrency and the digital economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-11-2019, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T17:27:36-07:00","id":1295984,"title":"","content":"Without wishing to distract, the reference to cryptocurrency and the digital economy made me think it more likely that the VAs would defect to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Back to the question, I'd probably guess that conventions wouldn't defect, the structure has gotten too tight for that since the VAs left. What you'd get is something closer to the way the Euthantos came together. Lots of little breakaway groups join different Traditions, only to ultimately find that they work better as an independent Tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T20:47:27-07:00","id":1296027,"title":"","content":"Craftmasons-Capitalism has a much weaker hold on humanity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T13:55:33-07:00","id":1296231,"title":"","content":"If the Syndicate left the Union, the Technocracy would collapse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T14:19:09-07:00","id":1296233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296231#post1296231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Syndicate left the Union, the Technocracy would collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not necessarily. It depends what proportion of the operatives and $$$ is transferred. The Union would be a lot weaker no matter how it shaked out, and I'm sure it would collapse almost instantly if the Syndicate were to leave with perfect unity and nothing going wrong for the traitors. My view is that the Syndicate would split in a sense; those who remained would join the New World Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T17:07:00-07:00","id":1296273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296231#post1296231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Syndicate left the Union, the Technocracy would collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly. It would likely be stronger than ever. The Syndicate is like a cancer that happens to do something useful. It's useful so you don't want to just cut it out, but it's still killing the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T20:01:55-07:00","id":1296315,"title":"","content":"You know. I do want to see a tradition version of the New World Order, but I have no idea what that would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T22:52:42-07:00","id":1296348,"title":"","content":"I have a real struggle seeing this happen. Parts of a convention might defect. It's easy to see any defect to the SoE or VA's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T06:03:13-07:00","id":1296382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296315#post1296315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know. I do want to see a tradition version of the New World Order, but I have no idea what that would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I couldn't really see them defecting over in the sense that they practically ARE the Union, being the political center that controls the masses and coordinates everything.<br /> <br /> If a faction of the NWO were to defect, it would probably be a faction committed to reality hacking, control of the masses and direction of media hypernarratives, political power etc. who have come to disagree fundamentally with the philosophy and direction of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So imagine all of the themes of the NWO, all of the typical paradigms and instruments, but instead focused on liberation, democracy, freedom, social revolutions... essentially the NWO with the &quot;technocratic&quot; (that is, undemocratic rule by experts and scientists) aspect removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T13:41:39-07:00","id":1296496,"title":"","content":"I could see the losing faction in the NWO/Syndicate war not necessarily leaving but becoming almost a 5th player in the Ascension War. Sure, they'd try to drum up allies but I'm not sure if this would be directly vying for ascension so much as wanting to remove another piece from the board. Syndicate members tend to make friends quickly and the NWO strikes me as a group that has some very useful things to offer.<br /> <br /> If the Syndicate were to leave, I'm not sure where that'd put the VEs. At the end of the day, the Technocracy simply has the better tools to protect reality.<br /> <br /> The NWO to me has the weakest implementation of Technomancy among the groups. I could see something where the NWO tries to firm up philosophical realism but subverting groups. One could blame the Traditions at least partially say for the antivax movement or religious extremism through the promotion of almost postmodern levels of relativism. I'm not saying they are responsible for this but you can lay out an argument to say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T17:16:51-07:00","id":1296543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296273#post1296273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not particularly. It would likely be stronger than ever. The Syndicate is like a cancer that happens to do something useful. It's useful so you don't want to just cut it out, but it's still killing the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see them as a cancer; I see them as <i>having</i> a cancer, just like every other Convention. But, just like every other Convention, they sense a vital role in the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T17:42:57-07:00","id":1296548,"title":"","content":"As for groups breaking away from the Technocracy, I don't see the break happening along Convention lines. Rather, I agree with the split that M20 has hinted at with Navalon and the talk of an upcoming purge and reorganization. Personally, I wouldn't call the breakaway faction \u201cNavalon\u201d; I would prefer that they reclaim \u201cthe Order of Reason\u201d. But the new Order of Reason would include expatriates from Iteration X, the Progenitors, the Void Engineers, the New World Order, and the Syndicate. <br /> <br /> And I don't see them joining the Traditions, either. I <i>can</i> see a greater willingness to work with the Traditions, with the Progenitors being the least interested in doing so and the Syndicate the most interested; but actually joining the Traditions? No, I don't see it happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:28:33-07:00","id":1296581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296543#post1296543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see them as a cancer; I see them as <i>having</i> a cancer, just like every other Convention. But, just like every other Convention, they sense a vital role in the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I See the SYndicate as Cancer.. like DEadpool has cancer. Its tuned them into a twisted parody of themself.. but its also the only thing keeping them alive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T05:03:09-07:00","id":1296654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295977-your-favourite-convention-defects-to-the-traditions-what-does-that-look-like?p=1296548#post1296548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for groups breaking away from the Technocracy, I don't see the break happening along Convention lines. Rather, I agree with the split that M20 has hinted at with Navalon and the talk of an upcoming purge and reorganization. Personally, I wouldn't call the breakaway faction \u201cNavalon\u201d; I would prefer that they reclaim \u201cthe Order of Reason\u201d. But the new Order of Reason would include expatriates from Iteration X, the Progenitors, the Void Engineers, the New World Order, and the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> And I don't see them joining the Traditions, either. I <i>can</i> see a greater willingness to work with the Traditions, with the Progenitors being the least interested in doing so and the Syndicate the most interested; but actually joining the Traditions? No, I don't see it happening.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the way I would go with it too. They aren't going to have the same dreams for humanity, but their dreams are closer to each other than they are to the purged Technocracy. It would actually be a lot like the state the Early Traditions were in, just without any kind of formal agreement. <br /> <br /> The Etherites and VAs broke away for reasons of independence and freedom of thought. That made them reasonable fit for the Traditions and also put them in a position where they needed allies to survive. The entire Technocracy breaking in two over differences in philosophy doesn't put quite the same pressures on either side. We shouldn't expect the same results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}